## Data flow cheat sheet

- **Calendar query:** `get_calendar_events` RPC (requires `p_user_id = auth.uid()`; enforced server-side) — returns the caller's own `user_events → events` (every event on your calendar is your copy), with "Shared by X" attribution via the most recent non-hidden incoming share, and a hide filter that suppresses events whose only incoming shares are from hidden people.
- **Create event:** `find_or_create_event` RPC → insert `user_events` → navigate to share screen → `share_event` RPC → `send-notification` (push + SMS) for new recipients.
- **Edit event:** `find_or_create_event` RPC (new snapshot) → UPDATE `user_events.event_id` → old snapshot untouched. On unique conflict (user already owns the target snapshot), merge shares onto the existing row and delete the old one.
- **Share event:** `share_event` RPC with the selected person ids — records `event_shares` and delivers each app-user recipient their own `user_events` copy; pending contacts get copies on sign-up. The share sheet is additive-only: existing shares render as "✓ Shared" and can't be deselected.
- **Remove event:** delete own `user_events` row (share records cascade). Purely personal — recipients keep their copies.
- **Hide a person:** insert `hidden_people` → events they shared disappear from the calendar and their shares no longer notify.

## Conventions

- Screens use `useFocusEffect` (not `useEffect`) for data fetching so lists refresh on navigation.
- Phone numbers are always stored in E.164 format (`+14165551234`).
- Supabase client is initialized in `lib/supabase.ts` with AsyncStorage for session persistence.
- All Supabase queries from the client go through RLS. Server-side operations use `SECURITY DEFINER` functions.
- Edge functions are locked down: `send-notification` and `og-metadata` require a valid user JWT (send-notification also verifies caller ownership of the `user_event`); `cleanup-people`/`cleanup-events` require the `CRON_SECRET` header and fail closed when unset.
- User-facing failures surface via `showError` or inline error + retry banners — not console-only. Expected auth mistakes (wrong/expired OTP, SMS rate limits, SMS send failure) use a short `showAlert` via `lib/authErrors.ts` (`getAuthUserMessage`); reserve `showError` for unexpected failures.
- OTP resend starts a 60s cooldown after the initial send (`sent=1` param from sign-in) and after each resend, so an accidental tap on "Try again" cannot fire a second SMS immediately.
- Never call `Alert.alert` directly (react-native-web makes it a no-op). Use `showAlert`/`showConfirm` from `lib/dialogs.ts` so dialogs also render in the browser via `window.alert`/`window.confirm`.
- Dates and phone numbers are formatted for display via `lib/format.ts` (`formatEventDate`, `formatPhoneDisplay`) — never render raw `YYYY-MM-DD` dates or E.164 numbers to users.
- Screens get their top padding from `useSafeAreaInsets()` (not hard-coded values), and multi-field forms wrap in `KeyboardAvoidingView`.
- Interactive elements carry `accessibilityRole` (plus `accessibilityLabel`/`accessibilityState` where the visible text isn't self-explanatory); touch targets are at least 44pt.
- Automated regression tests use Jest + React Native Testing Library (`npm test -- --runInBand`).
- Database semantics are tested by SQL tests: `bash supabase/tests/run_local.sh` spins up a scratch PostgreSQL with a mocked auth schema, applies every migration in order, and runs `supabase/tests/*.sql` assertions.
- E2E tests use Playwright (`npm run build:web && npm run test:e2e`) across desktop Chrome, Mobile Safari (WebKit), and Mobile Chrome; they sign in with the test-OTP accounts and must stay green. Test contexts disable `navigator.locks` (see `e2e/fixtures.ts`) — any context created outside the fixture needs `newExtraContext()`. Nav screens stay mounted when covered (use `visibleText`); modals overlay without hiding the base screen (scope to `getByRole('dialog')` and wait for unmount before touching what's underneath).
- Convention checks run via `npm run test:conventions` (`scripts/check-conventions.mjs`) in fast CI: accessibilityRole on touchables, no `Alert.alert` outside dialog helpers, no hard-coded hex colors. Exceptions carry an inline `conventions-ok` comment.
- Branching: agents push finished work straight to `staging` (fast checks must pass locally first); every push runs the full suite and redeploys the staging preview (`https://staging.shared-events.pages.dev`) when green. Promotion to `production` happens only when the owner says to ship — a fast-forward push of the green-tested staging tip, enforced by required checks on `production`. `docs/development-workflow.md` is the source of truth.
- Cloud manual testing should follow `manual-tests/cloud_manual_regression.md` (preflight via `npm run test:manual`).

